# SUSE

> SUSE is an open source enterprise software company providing Linux, cloud native, edge and AI infrastructure platforms. Core products include SUSE Linux Enterprise Server, SUSE Rancher Prime for Kubernetes management, SUSE Edge, and SUSE AI Factory for private enterprise AI.

SUSE products run on-premises, in public cloud, at the edge and in air-gapped environments, with a focus on interoperability, digital sovereignty and avoiding vendor lock-in. Technical documentation lives at documentation.suse.com, product downloads and subscription management at scc.suse.com, and support lifecycle information at suse.com/lifecycle.

For product version support dates, patches and errata, use the SUSE Customer Center and the Product Support Lifecycle pages rather than marketing pages.

## Products — Linux

- [SUSE Linux Enterprise Server](https://www.suse.com/products/server/): Enterprise Linux distribution for mission-critical workloads across physical, virtual, cloud and mainframe environments.
- [SUSE Linux Enterprise Server for SAP Applications](https://www.suse.com/products/sles-for-sap/): SLES variant optimized and certified for SAP and SAP HANA workloads.
- [SUSE Multi-Linux Support](https://www.suse.com/products/multi-linux-support/): Support for mixed Linux estates including non-SUSE distributions such as RHEL and CentOS.
- [SUSE Multi-Linux Manager](https://www.suse.com/products/multi-linux-manager/): Centralized patching, configuration and compliance management for large mixed Linux estates.
- [SUSE Linux Micro](https://www.suse.com/products/micro/): Immutable, lightweight Linux OS for containers and edge deployments.
- [Linux solutions overview](https://www.suse.com/solutions/linux/): Entry point for SUSE's Linux portfolio and positioning.

## Products — Cloud native and Kubernetes

- [SUSE Rancher Prime](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/): Enterprise Kubernetes management across hybrid and multi-cloud, including cluster lifecycle, policy and observability.
- [SUSE Virtualization](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/virtualization/): Open source hyperconverged virtualization for running VMs and containers on one platform; migration path from VMware.
- [VMware to SUSE Virtualization migration checklist](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/virtualization/migration-checklist/): Pre-migration, execution and post-migration checklist for moving VMware VMs to SUSE Virtualization, covering cold and warm migration and Coriolis automation.
- [SUSE Virtualization Interactive Labs](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/virtualization/interactive-labs/): Five guided click-through labs on SUSE Virtualization: UI, creating VMs, networking, storage and snapshots, and live migration; no setup required.
- [SUSE Storage](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/storage/): Cloud native block storage for Kubernetes, based on Longhorn.
- [SUSE Security](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/security/): Container and Kubernetes runtime security, formerly NeuVector.
- [SUSE Observability](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/observability/): Monitoring and troubleshooting for Kubernetes environments.
- [SUSE Application Collection](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/application-collection/): Curated, signed container images and Helm charts for enterprise use.
- [SUSE Rancher for AWS](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher/aws/): Rancher Prime deployed and supported on AWS.
- [SUSE Rancher for SAP Applications](https://www.suse.com/products/rancher-for-sap/): Kubernetes platform configured for SAP workloads.
- [SUSE Cloud Observability](https://www.suse.com/products/cloud/observability/): Observability for cloud and hybrid infrastructure.
- [Cloud native solutions overview](https://www.suse.com/solutions/cloud-native/): Entry point for the cloud native portfolio.

## Products — Edge

- [SUSE Edge](https://www.suse.com/products/edge/): Edge platform for distributed, resource-constrained and intermittently connected sites.
- [SUSE Industrial Edge](https://www.suse.com/products/industrial-edge/): Edge computing for manufacturing and industrial environments.
- [SUSE Telco Cloud](https://www.suse.com/products/edge-for-telco/): Carrier-grade platform for telco network functions and RAN workloads.
- [Edge solutions overview](https://www.suse.com/solutions/edge/): Entry point for edge positioning and use cases.

## Products — AI

- [SUSE AI Factory](https://www.suse.com/products/ai/): Private enterprise AI platform for running generative AI and MLOps workloads inside your own perimeter.
- [SUSE AI Factory with NVIDIA](https://www.suse.com/products/ai/factory-with-nvidia/): AI Factory validated and deployed on NVIDIA accelerated infrastructure.
